# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-09-11 (Aditya). The rules above miss the formats we actually have
# on disk. Sizes are real, measured in C:\maritime-data:
#
#   gdp_hourly_..._20190101-20240101.csv    108.8 MB  <- GitHub HARD-REJECTS >100 MB
#   gdp_hourly_..._20210101-20260101.csv     50.4 MB  <- would have bloated history forever
#
# A committed large file stays in history even after deletion, so this has to be
# right BEFORE the first `git add`, not after.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
*.npy
*.npz

# Environment / tooling
.venv*/
env/.venv/
.uv/
.python-version
.env
*.pem
*.key
.vscode/
.idea/

# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
# Never commit: the cluster password, SSH private keys, or any API credential
# (R3g). ARCO-ERA5 needs no credential at all -- it is anonymous -- so there is
# nothing to leak from the wind pipeline by design.

# Third-party screenshots (Zoom Earth etc.) are visual references we do not own
# and should not redistribute from a public repo. They stay in the vault.
figures/reference/

# Figures: report figures ARE tracked on purpose -- they are small deliverables
# and FIGURES.md records what each one argues. Scratch plots are not.
figures/scratch/
figures/tmp/
